WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:06.420
He-Man's first foray into theaters in 1987
didn't exactly go as planned, but the once-mighty

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.260
TV and toy phenomenon is finally poised to
get the reboot treatment.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.580
Even though the first movie was a flop, the
new Masters of the Universe is far more likely

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.600
to blow you away.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.500
Here's why.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.380
To say that the 1987 film Masters of the Universe
was a bit of a disappointment would be a massive

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.200
understatement.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.830
The movie starred Dolph Lundgren as He-Man,
Frank Langella as the villainous Skeletor,

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:32.420
and a young Courteney Cox as a newly introduced
Earthling character named Julia Winston.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.120
Cox's character, in a way, embodied many fans'
major problems with the film.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.430
There wasn't anything wrong with the future
Friends star's performance, per se, but her

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:45.720
having such a key role in the film left fans
hugely frustrated — for two reasons.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.270
First, Julia is from Earth — which is also
where most of the film takes place.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.760
By contrast, the cartoon and comics were based
on the planet Eternia, a fantastical land

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.780
that combined elements of sword and sorcery
with science fiction.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.260
By taking He-Man out of that familiar setting
and transporting him to Earth, the movie was

00:01:03.269 --> 00:01:07.280
forced to tell a fish-out-of-water story that
prevented fans from getting to experience

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.460
He-Man in his element.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.259
Secondly, Julia Winston never appeared in
the cartoon, the comics, or the toy line.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.380
She was a character created solely for the
film, and she wasn't the only one.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.320
Despite having dozens of well-liked and fascinating
characters at their disposal, the filmmakers

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.560
chose to forego them all in favor of their
own like keyboard-playing Kevin.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.320
"What do you think?"

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.960
"Sounds great."

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:35.740
The creative team behind the new Masters of
the Universe surely know just what went wrong

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.400
with the original, and there's no way they're
going to repeat the mistakes of the past.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:40.460
Sorry, Kevin.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:46.420
It may be 2019, but these days you'd be forgiven
for thinking it was actually 1989.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.400
Everywhere you look in pop culture, the decade
of big hair, neon clothing, and Reaganomics

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.640
seems to be taking over.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.750
Just look at what's on TV these days: Modern
reboots of classic '80s series MacGyver and

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:03.259
Magnum P.I. are both important blocks of CBS'
primetime lineup, while ABC's comedy lineup

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:08.940
is partly anchored by the '80s-set The Goldbergs
and The Conners, a continuation of '80s hit

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:09.440
Roseanne.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.580
On top of all that, Netflix has a Voltron
reboot, the Full House follow-up Fuller House,

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:19.110
'80s wrestling drama GLOW, and, of course,
the massively popular Stranger Things, which

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:23.300
even got Coca-Cola to bring back New Coke
— one of the biggest product failures of

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.700
all time — as a tie-in.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.140
Netflix also produces She-Ra and the Princesses
of Power, a reboot of He-Man's female-focused

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:32.620
spinoff series, which debuted in 1985.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:37.140
If anything, the movie industry is even more
in love with the '80s.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.850
2019 alone has seen reboots of Child's Play
and Pet Sematary, with new sequels for The

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.780
Terminator and Rambo on the way.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.980
In 2020, things are going to get even more
retro — with belated sequels for Ghostbusters,

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.400
Bill &amp; Ted, Coming to America, and Top Gun
all slated for release.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.780
Even the upcoming Wonder Woman sequel takes
place in the '80s, and they're not even being

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:01.000
subtle with that one — the film is literally
called Wonder Woman: 1984.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:05.760
People just can't get enough of the '80s right
now, which means the time is ripe for a reboot

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.540
of one of the decade's most iconic contributions
to pop culture.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:16.360
Noah Centineo probably isn't who most Masters
of the Universe fans had in mind for the role

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:16.880
of He-Man.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.560
The young actor has dark hair instead of Prince
Adam's signature blond, for example.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:25.060
He's also fairly slight of build and lacks
a bodybuilder's physique.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.440
On top of that, he's only 23 years old.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:33.800
That means Centineo was born in 1996 — long
after He-Man had his moment in the sun.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:38.480
But despite his appearance not quite matching
cartoon He-Man's and his relative youth, Centineo

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.590
is who Sony Pictures cast for the lead role
in the new Masters of the Universe.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.800
And believe it or not, they seem to have known
exactly what they were doing.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:51.180
Centineo may not look much like He-Man, but
he is poised to deliver a memorable performance

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.800
as the character nonetheless.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:58.060
Centineo burst onto the scene in a big way
in 2018 thanks to his role in the Netflix

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:02.890
teen romance To All the Boys I’ve Loved
Before, before appearing in two more films

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:06.560
for the streaming giant: Sierra Burgess Is
a Loser and The Perfect Date.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:10.960
Thanks to his charismatic performances in
these films, Centineo has become something

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.820
of an internet sensation, and his likability
factor will likely go a long way toward helping

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.640
him sell his incarnation of He-Man.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:21.220
And it's happened before, too: just take a
look at Chris Pratt.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:26.040
He wasn't anyone's idea of a typical action
hero when he was playing chubby slacker Andy

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:31.390
Dwyer on Parks &amp; Recreation, but his performance
as Star-Lord in Guardians of the Galaxy completely

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:35.220
changed people's perception of him — and
now he's one of the world's biggest action

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:35.720
stars.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.820
Expect Centineo to undergo a similar transformation.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:43.360
And sure, he can work out and throw on a wig
to pull off the look of He-Man, but what's

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.390
really going to make his performance memorable
is star quality.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.260
Luckily, he's got that in spades.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:53.040
Two of the hottest genres in pop culture right
now are science fiction and fantasy.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:57.390
For the past several years, the box office
is dominated by the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.460
which has been trending more and more toward
straight-up science fiction.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:05.620
Avengers: Endgame deals with time travel,
aliens, and all kinds of intergalactic insanity,

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.060
And, of course, another sci-fi film, Avatar,
was the top box office earner worldwide before

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.120
Endgame took the crown.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.920
On television, fantasy is in vogue, with the
series finale of Game of Thrones recently

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.360
becoming the most-watched episode of any show
in HBO history.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.680
And with multiple Game of Thrones spinoffs
in the works, along with adaptations of Lord

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:29.050
of the Rings and The Wheel of Time, it seems
like fantasy will continue to dominate TV

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:30.100
for years to come.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:34.580
But it's when you successfully blend these
two genres that the real magic happens.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:36.580
"Surprise!"

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.060
Thor: Ragnarok managed to pull this off with
aplomb.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.140
By taking Thor, the most fantasy-friendly
Marvel character, and putting him in a retro

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:48.460
science-fiction environment, the movie came
up with something truly special and unique.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.480
Except, of course, it wasn't all that unique,
because He-Man and the Masters of the Universe

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.260
was doing it 35 years earlier.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:01.100
He-Man is about a society on the planet Eternia
where magic and alien technology exist together

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.640
and are employed equally.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:07.600
He-Man may wield a magic sword and hang out
with a sorceress, but he also sometimes flies

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.260
a ship that shoots lasers.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:13.720
Fantasy and sci-fi can be tons of fun when
they're mixed together, and given the franchise's

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:18.080
long-established history of doing just that,
the new Masters of the Universe movie ought

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.040
to be a blast.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.440
Look, not everyone likes He-Man.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:24.140
That's fair.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.520
Prince Adam is kind of a dork, and He-Man
himself is kind of just a buff guy with a

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.440
bad haircut and no personality.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:35.460
But, like the 1987 original, this new movie
isn't called "He-Man," it's called "Masters

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.440
of the Universe."

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:37.800
Masters, plural.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:42.580
He-Man is part of an Avengers-like squad that
fights evil, and each one of them is more

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:43.760
awesome than the last.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:49.860
There's Man-At-Arms, who's a master at every
weapon and has a sick mustache; Teela, a unicorn-riding

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:54.270
goddess; and Battle Cat, the armored steed
that Prince Adam's cowardly tiger Cringer

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.820
turns into whenever Adam becomes He-Man.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:00.780
And as cool as the heroes of the franchise
are, the villains are even better.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:06.520
Battling against He-Man for the power of Castle
Grayskull are evildoers like Beast Man, a

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:11.810
hulking monster; Evil-Lyn, a magic wand-wielding
sorceress with a pun for a name; and Trap

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:16.720
Jaw, a cyborg with sharp metal teeth and an
arm that can be swapped out for numerous weapons.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:21.200
All of these bad guys act as henchmen for
Skeletor, one of the most iconic villains

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.760
in all of genre fiction.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:28.139
Skeletor is a diabolical blue-skinned brute
with a skull for a head and an unquenchable

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.020
lust for power.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.570
For many, he's the best part of Masters of
the Universe, and seeing him adapted onto

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:37.920
the big screen using today's technology will
be worth the price of admission all on its

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:38.420
own.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:44.220
As you've probably figured out by now, Masters
of the Universe is a pretty fantastical franchise,

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:47.460
full of all kinds of magic powers, battles,
heroes and villains.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.740
Oh, and a castle shaped like a skull.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:54.510
Of course, it was relatively easy to show
all of these things in animated form in the

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.540
1980s, because all you had to do was draw
them.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.700
But bringing it all to life convincingly in
a live-action movie was always going to be

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.480
a far more difficult task.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:07.810
In the '80s, CGI was practically unheard of
and most movies were still using puppetry

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:09.660
and other practical effects.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:14.860
Puppetry can be fun and definitely has a strong
nostalgia factor nowadays, but it typically

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.560
isn't the most convincing visual effect modern
movies have at their disposal.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:23.420
Over the past few years, however, CGI has
finally reached the point where it can create

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:28.000
entire worlds and characters that are virtually
indistinguishable from real life.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:33.440
In Avengers: Infinity War and its sequel Endgame,
for instance, the villain Thanos is completely

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.640
computer and motion capture-generated.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:38.940
Despite all that, however, he still feels
like a real character.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:43.570
His facial expressions and other movements
are incredibly lifelike, and at no point in

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:46.280
either of those movies does he ever feel artificial.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:51.060
Using this technology will be the key to creating
a convincing Eternia, and the prospect of

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.860
seeing the planet come to life like never
before is very exciting indeed.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.900
Post-credits scenes have become something
of a given with big blockbusters over the

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:05.980
past decade, thanks largely to Marvel popularizing
the trend, but they've actually been around

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:06.620
for far longer.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:11.200
And although they were rare at the time, post-credits
scenes would still occasionally pop up in

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:16.470
some 1980s films — mostly used in comedies
to squeeze in one more joke, like in 1980's

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:22.520
Airplane!, 1987's Planes, Trains, and Automobiles,
and 1986's Ferris Bueller's Day Off, which

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.700
had one of the most memorable of the decade.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:26.860
You're still here?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:30.980
It’s over.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:34.060
Go home."

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:39.180
But then there was the post-credits scene
in the original Masters of the Universe — which

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.380
remains one of the most notorious ever made.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:47.140
Near the end of the film, He-Man and Skeletor
engage in a final battle that ends when He-Man

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:50.160
knocks Skeletor into an unfathomably deep
pit.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:53.880
Skeletor is presumed dead, and the film ends
on a happy note.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.540
So far, so normal, right?

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.700
Well, after the credits have rolled, this
happens.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.400
"I'll be back!"

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.730
It's a tantalizing — if slightly lame — promise,
and one which was doubtless made by a bunch

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:14.240
of filmmakers who were confident they'd one
day be producing a sequel.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:17.280
But, in the end, it turned out that Skeletor
lied.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:22.180
Because the film was a massive critical and
box office failure, no sequel was ever produced,

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.300
making Skeletor's tease at the end of the
film utterly pointless.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:29.490
But now, with the new Masters of the Universe
on the way, Skeletor will finally make his

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:33.770
long-awaited return to the silver screen — and
the character will be able to keep his promise

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.240
after all these years.

